ls like a spiral to the beast, which kind of should. But it might be a wrong impression, I confess.<br /> <br /> I liked the Harano Hauglosk in W5, but if it was like they did in V6 it would've been better.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T13:35:29-07:00","id":1564309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564295-is-backporting-v6-humainty-into-w5-a-good-idea?p=1564305#post1564305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, while I found it interesting, the new Humanity system is definitely a new direction. Since both poles are considered reflexes of one another now, instead of a 1 to 10 line. It does feels like a Werewolf stuff.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that's kinda because it seems new versions of humanity is inspired by werewolf the forsaken 2e's harmony bar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-23T10:25:22-07:00","id":1564932,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25848\" data-vbnamecard=\"25848\">MrornX</a> <br /> <br /> The best WoDs for me are the ones that steal and work with ideas done in CoD. I just find CoD too heavy and hard system-wise to use it frequently. But the concepts and mechanical solutions are amazing; that is why I respect CoD so much, it tried to do thing different, more planned and tightly put. 5th edition systems best features owe a lot to CoD in my opinion.<br /> <br /> I never wanted to play Werewolf Apocalpyse or Hunter Reckoning before their 5th edition iterations. <br /> While I find absurd that they seem to have abandon other splats for the 5th edition and are jumping to the 6th, at least V6 is also trying new stuff (even if I find mostly detractive, there is some pretty cool things). The Humanity scale is not my favorite version of what Humanity is, but it is an interesting system to work with, and it does feel more at home with splats like Werewolf and Changeling, where ballance is more important than resisting the donward spiral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-28T06:16:02-07:00","id":1565018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564295-is-backporting-v6-humainty-into-w5-a-good-idea#post1564295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So anyone thinking about back porting New Humanity system back to W5. I feel like it's more appropriate for WtA anyway since V6 version of Humanity blatantly takes inspiration from werewolf the Forsaken 2E's harmony bar since they both centered around balancing between two ends of a bar. Though V6 arguably improves on Harmony since going towards either ends does offer buffs rather than just managing debuffs.<br /> <br /> Like you could easily reframe Harano and Hauglosk into something similar to the new Humanity bar. with the bat could the bar easily represent a balancing act between two extreme reaction a garou would have to the current state of the world, where Hauglosk is the urge to act and Harano is refection on they own actions.<br /> <br /> Ideally Harano should temper Hauglosk while Hauglosk should rouse a garou from Harano and falling into either end of the bar would bring ruin to the garou.<br /> <br /> Or it could just easily be a simple Calm/Rage bar.That could also work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From what I've seen of V6's Humanity system so far, it seems to be more of a highly personalized concept this time around. You're not struggling to uphold some codified set of ethics, but rather trying to hold onto who you were as a person before your embrace.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how that would work for Garou, since they have a dualistic nature? It's not the Man and Wolf competing against each other for control of the body, Garou are both human and wolf merged into a single creature; and they must learn to achieve a harmonious balance, rather than favoring one aspect over the other.<br /> <br /> <br /> Making it a calm / rage bar feels weird, since Garou are directly empowered by their Rage, and often have to spend it to utilize their supernatural abilities. This means you would constantly have to tip the bar towards Hauglosk in order to do anything Garou related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}